card.statement:
Let $G$ be a directed graph with vertices $1,2,\dots,n$ and no undirected cycles. By a $G$-canonical matrix pair we mean a matrix pair of the form

\begin{equation*}
\left(\begin{bmatrix}
\lambda _1 &&0 \\
&\ddots& \\
0&&\lambda _r
\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}
b_{11} &\dots&b_{1r} \\
\vdots&\ddots&\vdots \\
b_{r1}&\dots&b_{rr}
\end{bmatrix}\right),\qquad \lambda_1\prec\dots\prec
\lambda_r,
\end{equation*}

in which every entry $b_{pq}$ satisfies the following conditions:

- [(i)] $b_{pq}=1$ if $G$ has the directed edge $p\to q$;

- [(ii)] $b_{pq}=0$ if either $G$ has no undirected path from $p$ to $q$, or the undirected path from $p$ to $q$ contains a directed edge $i\to
      j$ such that $(i,j)\succ
      (p,q)$ with respect to the lexicographic order;

- [(iii)] $b_{pq}$ is arbitrary, otherwise.
